---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { api } from '../lib/api';
import { usd, pct } from '../lib/format';

const [report, meta, network] = await Promise.all([api.alpha(90), api.meta(), api.network()]);
const sweeps = (report?.sweeps ?? []).slice(0, 8);
const best = report?.best ?? null;
// The "do nothing" baseline: cash sits still and earns nothing.
const workingYield = report && report.venues.length ? Math.max(...report.venues.map((v) => v.mean_apy)) : 0;
const perfectTiming = report ? (report.upper_bound_usd / 1000) * 100 : 0; // % on $1,000 over the window
const realistic = best ? best.alpha_bps_per_year / 100 : 0;
const years = (report?.window_days ?? 90) / 365;
---
<Base
  title="What is choosing the better venue actually worth?"
  subtitle="We measured the claim before building the product on it. Two verified dollar venues on Stellar, daily rates from a public feed, and a rule that only reacts to yesterday's data — the same restraint the product uses with your money."
  network={network}
  meta={meta}
  updated={report?.generated_at ?? null}
>
  {!report ? (
    <div class="card err"><h2>This report is unavailable right now</h2><p class="small">Please try again in a moment.</p></div>
  ) : (
    <>
      <div class="grid g4">
        <div class="card stat">
          <span class="k">Cash sitting still</span>
          <span class="v num hero">0%</span>
          <span class="note small muted">what an idle dollar earns</span>
        </div>
        <div class="card stat">
          <span class="k">Money at work</span>
          <span class="v num hero">{pct(workingYield, 1)}</span>
          <span class="note small muted">a year, in a verified venue</span>
        </div>
        <div class="card stat">
          <span class="k">Perfect timing · {report.window_days} days</span>
          <span class="v num">+{perfectTiming.toFixed(2)}%</span>
          <span class="note small muted">{usd(report.upper_bound_usd, 2)} on $1,000 over {report.window_days} days, with perfect foresight</span>
        </div>
        <div class="card stat">
          <span class="k">A patient rule · per year</span>
          <span class="v num">{best ? `${realistic >= 0 ? '+' : ''}${realistic.toFixed(2)}%` : '—'}</span>
          <span class="note small muted">{best ? `${usd(best.alpha_usd, 2)} on $1,000 · ${best.switches} moves` : ''} — the rest cannot be known in advance</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card stack">
        <h2>The two venues, side by side</h2>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Venue</th><th class="right">Days measured</th><th class="right">Average rate</th><th class="right">Lowest</th><th class="right">Highest</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {report.venues.map((v) => (
              <tr>
                <td>{v.label}</td>
                <td class="right num">{v.days}</td>
                <td class="right num strong">{pct(v.mean_apy)}</td>
                <td class="right num muted">{pct(v.min_apy)}</td>
                <td class="right num muted">{pct(v.max_apy)}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="small muted">
          Staying in <strong>{report.best_single_label}</strong> the whole time turns $1,000 into {usd(report.best_single_usd, 2)}.
          Moving at exactly the right moment would have turned it into {usd(report.perfect_hindsight_usd, 2)}.
          That difference — {usd(report.upper_bound_usd, 2)} — is the whole value of moving money around, and nobody can
          capture all of it, because it requires knowing tomorrow.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card stack">
        <h2>How patient is the right answer?</h2>
        <p class="small muted">
          We tested every combination of two settings: how long we wait between moves, and how much better a venue has
          to be before it is worth the move. The best combination is the one we ship.
        </p>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Wait between moves</th><th>Improvement needed</th><th class="right">Moves</th>
              <th class="right">$1,000 ends at</th><th class="right">Versus staying put</th><th class="right">Per year</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {sweeps.map((s) => (
              <tr class={best && s.cooldown_days === best.cooldown_days && s.threshold_bps === best.threshold_bps ? 'best' : ''}>
                <td class="num">{s.cooldown_days} days</td>
                <td class="num">{(s.threshold_bps / 100).toFixed(2)}%</td>
                <td class="right num">{s.switches}</td>
                <td class="right num">{usd(s.final_usd, 2)}</td>
                <td class={`right num ${s.alpha_usd > 0 ? 'pos' : 'neg'}`}>{usd(s.alpha_usd, 2)}</td>
                <td class="right num">{s.alpha_bps_per_year >= 0 ? '+' : ''}{(s.alpha_bps_per_year / 100).toFixed(2)}%</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="small muted">
          The gap between the two venues was wide on {report.days_gap_over_threshold} of {report.window_days} days —
          {(report.avg_gap_bps / 100).toFixed(2)}% on average. That looks like easy money until you notice it is
          mostly one venue being briefly cheap: a rule that chases every gap pays for it in moves, and sometimes moves
          into the weaker venue just as it turns.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card stack callout">
        <h2>What we changed because of this</h2>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>We do not sell "the highest rate".</strong> Between two verified venues, moving well is worth a fraction of a percent a year at ordinary sizes. Real, but not a reason to download an app.</li>
          <li><strong>The value is 0% → {pct(workingYield, 1)}.</strong> Idle cash earning nothing is the actual problem. Add the ability to leave at any time and to see what you hold, and that is the product.</li>
          <li><strong>We wait two days between moves, not seven.</strong> Measured leadership between these venues lasts about a week; a seven-day wait misses most of it.</li>
          <li><strong>We ignore outliers.</strong> One venue printed 193% for a single day. A naive rule chases it; we treat it as a liquidity squeeze, drop the day, and stop sending new money there.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="small muted">Past performance is not a forecast. Rates move; the discipline does not.</p>
      </div>

      <details class="card stack tech">
        <summary>Method, for the curious</summary>
        <p class="small">
          Daily rates from the public DefiLlama yields feed over {report.window_days} days ({years.toFixed(2)} of a year).
          Observations above three times their trailing 30-day median are dropped before anything is computed.
          A move is decided on the previous day's observation and applied the next day — no peeking at the future.
          Transaction costs are excluded because a move costs under a cent on Stellar.
        </p>
        <p class="small">
          The table above sweeps waiting periods of one to seven days against improvement thresholds of 0% to 1%,
          replaying the same window for each combination; the shipped policy is the highest-returning combination that
          keeps the number of moves sensible. Recompute it with <span class="mono">GET /api/v1/alpha?days=90</span>.
        </p>
      </details>
    </>
  )}
</Base>

<style>
  .stat { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 3px; }
  .k { font-size: 11px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--muted); }
  .v { font-size: 26px; font-weight: 700; }
  .hero { color: var(--brand); }
  .stack { margin-top: 14px; }
  .strong { font-weight: 600; }
  .pos { color: var(--brand); }
  .neg { color: var(--bad); }
  tr.best { background: #F1F7EE; }
  tr.best td { font-weight: 600; }
  .callout { background: #F6FBF4; border-color: #D6E3CF; }
  .callout ol { margin: 0 0 10px 18px; padding: 0; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.7; color: #4A3D2C; }
  .tech summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); }
  .tech[open] summary { margin-bottom: 12px; color: var(--ink); }
  .err { border-color: #E7C4B6; }
</style>
